      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\n`dist_checkpointing.dict_utils.diff()` reports tensors with different shapes as equal when they broadcast. It compares with `torch.all(x1 == x2)`, so:\n\n```python\ndiff({\"w\": torch.ones(1, 4)}, {\"w\": torch.ones(8, 4)})  # ([], [], [])  - no mismatch\ndiff({\"w\": torch.zeros(4)}, {\"w\": torch.zeros(4, 1)})   # ([], [], [])  - no mismatch\n```\n\n`diff()` backs the cross-rank common state dict check (`validation.py`, `_validate_common_state_dict`) and many checkpoint round-trip tests, so a tensor saved with the wrong shape can pass them silently.\n\nThis PR checks shapes before comparing values. A shape difference is reported as a mismatch, with both shapes added to the debug data. Tensors with equal shapes are compared exactly as before.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none. This is a small bug fix. #7743 fixes a different bug in the same function (the path prefix for extra sequence elements); the two changes don't overlap.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel (...), I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test (N/A: no kernel changes)\n- [x] I have added proper typing to my code (no signature changes)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation (N/A)\n- [x] I have run the autoformatter on my PR\n\n### Testing\n\nNew test in `tests/unit_tests/dist_checkpointing/test_validation.py`: `[1, 4]` vs `[8, 4]`, `[4]` vs `[4, 1]`, and `[]` vs `[3]` must be reported as mismatches, and equal tensors must still compare equal.\n\n```\nPYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest -q tests/unit_tests/dist_checkpointing/test_validation.py\n```\n\n- Without the fix: the new test fails.\n- With the fix: 2 passed.\n- black (`--skip-magic-trailing-comma --skip-string-normalization`), isort, ruff and pylint (10.00/10) are clean.\n\nI tested on CPU only, with PyTorch 2.14.1. I could not run the GPU checkpoint tests that call `diff()`; if any of them relies on two differently shaped tensors comparing equal, CI will show it here.\n\nThis change was prepared with AI assistance (Claude Code).\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
